url: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24078477
abstract: >
  AetherRuntime is the sixth functional dimension (provisional) of the
  Aether family. It investigates whether a runtime-assurance gap genuinely
  exists in the Aether family, and specifies a five-layer architecture
  (monitoring, detection, containment, halt, recovery) with two
  propositions (determinism of local anomaly detection; irreducible halt
  window). No implementation is claimed. No real-world deployment has
  been evaluated. F1-F4 are not falsified by argument; F5 is untested.
